# Line endings. Git stores LF in the repository and checks out LF on every platform, so a
# contributor on Windows and one on Linux produce identical diffs. Without this, core.autocrlf
# decides per machine and a file touched on Windows comes back as a whole-file change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they fail to run; state it explicitly rather than relying on the
# rule above surviving a future edit to this file.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated lockfiles: keep them out of diffs and language statistics. They are still committed
# and still reviewed, just collapsed by default in pull requests.
**/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff

# Signed test vectors are computed by openssl, not written by hand. A diff of one line of these
# is noise; regenerate with the make_vectors scripts instead of editing.
skills/**/examples/fixtures/vectors.json linguist-generated=true
